# Smallbird Local — personal desktop build
#
# This app needs no build-time environment variables to run. Every API key
# — your AI provider (OpenAI/Anthropic/Gemini), Groq (speech-to-text), and
# Deepgram (text-to-speech) — is entered at runtime through
# Settings -> API Keys and stored securely in Windows Credential Manager —
# never in a .env file, never in source, never committed.
#
# This file only documents optional TIMING overrides, which genuinely are
# read from the process environment (not .env — Tauri/Rust here do not load
# .env files, so copying this to .env alone does nothing; set these as real
# process environment variables if you want to change them).
#
# GROQ_TIMEOUT_MS=15000
#   Optional. How long to wait for one Groq transcription request
#   (src-tauri/src/stt/groq.rs) before giving up on that utterance.
#
# Deepgram Flux TTS (src-tauri/src/tts/deepgram_flux.rs) has no equivalent
# timeout override — it's a persistent wss:// session per answer, not one
# bounded HTTP request per sentence, so there's no single request duration
# to cap.
#
# STT_END_SILENCE_MS / STT_VAD_GATE_ENABLED / STT_NUM_THREADS / STT_MODEL_DIR
# / STT_READY_TIMEOUT_MS
#   Optional local voice-activity/endpoint-detection tuning knobs — see
#   src-tauri/src/stt/sidecar.rs. Independent of the Groq API key: this
#   local engine only decides *when* you've stopped speaking, it never
#   produces the transcript text itself.
